  cites Shell chapter PowerShellEmit

 We say:

Section: Parameters

 -Kernel carries the doc block because the default is the trap: compile.ps1
 falls back to build-output/bare-metal/Codex.cdx, which holds whichever
 kernel ran LAST, so a check that omits it can judge the OLD compiler and
 report that nothing changed.

  ce-kernel-doc : List Text = ["The compiler to judge. Empty means compile.ps1's own default, which is", "build-output/bare-metal/Codex.cdx and therefore whichever kernel ran", "LAST. Every caller inside a gate passes this explicitly."]

  ce-params : List ShellParam = [sh-doc ce-kernel-doc (sh-param-default "Kernel" SptString (SeLit "")), sh-param-default "Jobs" SptInt (SeInt 4)]

Section: S01

  s01 : List ShellCmd = [ScRaw "Set-StrictMode -Version Latest", ScRaw "$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'", ScRaw "Set-Location (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot '..')", ScRaw "[Environment]::CurrentDirectory = (Get-Location).Path", ScBlank, ScComment "176 tests assert a REFUSAL, and until 2026-08-17 the gate ran 13 of them.", ScComment "", ScComment "codex/test/errors is the diagnostic path: each source is a program the", ScComment "compiler must reject, and its .failing names the codes that must fire. The", ScComment "set is reachable only from build/test.ps1, which is the battery and refuses", ScComment "to run without Damian. bvt.ps1 carries thirteen by name. So a rejection that", ScComment "stopped happening, or started happening for a different reason, was caught", ScComment "by nothing an agent is allowed to run.", ScComment "", ScComment "That is not hypothetical. bounded-exceeded declared `bounded linear` over a", ScComment "loop appending a text LITERAL; COMPILER-8 made that extend in place, rule 3", ScComment "stopped inferring it growing, the declaration held, and the test compiled", ScComment "clean -- the exact opposite of what it exists to assert. It reached main", ScComment "green in Update 45 and was found by a release battery, not by a gate.", ScComment "", ScComment "The set is derived from the directory, never listed here. A hand-maintained", ScComment "list is how the thirteen came to stand for a hundred and seventy-six.", ScComment "", ScComment "Exit 1 on any test that compiles, that fails with the wrong codes, or that", ScComment "declares nothing at all.", ScBlank, ScRaw "$errDir = Join-Path 'codex' (Join-Path 'test' 'errors')", ScRaw "if (-not (Test-Path -PathType Container $errDir)) {", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"FAIL: $errDir is missing\"", ScRaw "    exit 1", ScRaw "}", ScBlank, ScRaw "$tests = @(Get-ChildItem $errDir -Filter *.codex -File | ForEach-Object { $_.FullName } | Sort-Object)", ScRaw "if ($tests.Count -eq 0) {", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"FAIL: no tests under $errDir -- a check over an empty set passes for free\"", ScRaw "    exit 1", ScRaw "}", ScBlank]

Section: S02

  s02 : List ShellCmd = [ScRaw "$outRoot = Join-Path 'test-output' '_errors'", ScRaw "if (Test-Path $outRoot) { Remove-Item -Recurse -Force $outRoot }", ScRaw "New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $outRoot | Out-Null", ScBlank, ScRaw "$sw = [System.Diagnostics.Stopwatch]::StartNew()", ScRaw "Write-Host \"  check-errors: $($tests.Count) refusals, $Jobs parallel slots\"", ScBlank, ScRaw "$compileScript = Join-Path (Resolve-Path .).Path 'build\\compile.ps1'", ScRaw "$bad = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentBag[string]]::new()", ScRaw "$skipped = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentBag[string]]::new()", ScRaw "$passed = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentBag[string]]::new()", ScBlank, ScRaw "$tests | ForEach-Object -ThrottleLimit $Jobs -Parallel {", ScRaw "    $t = $_", ScRaw "    $base = [System.IO.Path]::GetFileNameWithoutExtension($t)", ScRaw "    $skipFile = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.skip'", ScRaw "    if (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $skipFile) {", ScRaw "        ($using:skipped).Add(\"$base ($((Get-Content -TotalCount 1 $skipFile).Trim()))\")", ScRaw "        return", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $failFile = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.failing'", ScRaw "    if (-not (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $failFile)) {", ScRaw "        ($using:bad).Add(\"$base -- no .failing sidecar: the test asserts nothing\")", ScRaw "        return", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $codes = @(Get-Content $failFile | ForEach-Object { $_.Trim() } | Where-Object { $_ })", ScRaw "    if ($codes.Count -eq 0) {", ScRaw "        ($using:bad).Add(\"$base -- .failing is empty: the test asserts nothing\")", ScRaw "        return", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $outDir = Join-Path $using:outRoot $base", ScRaw "    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $outDir | Out-Null", ScRaw "    $cdxOut = Join-Path $outDir \"$base.cdx\"", ScRaw "    $logOut = Join-Path $outDir \"$base.log\"", ScRaw "    # NOT $args: that is an automatic variable, and assigning it inside a", ScRaw "    # scriptblock shadows the one splatting reads.", ScRaw "    $cargs = @('-Src', $t, '-Out', $cdxOut, '-Log', $logOut)", ScRaw "    if ($using:Kernel) { $cargs += @('-Kernel', $using:Kernel) }", ScRaw "    & pwsh -NoProfile -File $using:compileScript @cargs *> $null", ScRaw "    if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {", ScRaw "        ($using:bad).Add(\"$base -- COMPILED, and it must be refused ($($codes -join ' '))\")", ScRaw "        return", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $logText = if (Test-Path $logOut) { Get-Content $logOut -Raw } else { '' }", ScRaw "    # test.ps1's adjudication, and it must stay identical to it: `error", ScRaw "    # (CDX)?0*<n>` rather than a bare CDX<n> search, because the lexer's codes", ScRaw "    # print unprefixed and single-digit (`error 6:`) and a CDX-prefixed search", ScRaw "    # reports those as wrong-code failures. A bare `CDX2031` checks only that", ScRaw "    # the code fired; `CDX2031@33:5` also pins WHERE, which a bare code cannot", ScRaw "    # -- a diagnostic reported at a synthetic 0,0 span prints no line:column", ScRaw "    # prefix at all, so a code-only check passes against a compiler that lost", ScRaw "    # the position entirely.", ScRaw "    $missing = ''", ScRaw "    foreach ($code in $codes) {", ScRaw "        if ($code -match '^(?<c>(CDX)?\\d+)@(?<l>\\d+):(?<col>\\d+)$') {", ScRaw "            $c = $matches['c'] -replace '^CDX', ''", ScRaw "            $pat = \"\\b$($matches['l']):$($matches['col']):\\s*error (CDX)?0*$c\\b\"", ScRaw "            if ($logText -notmatch $pat) { $missing = $code; break }", ScRaw "        } elseif ($logText -notmatch \"error (CDX)?0*$code\\b\") { $missing = $code; break }", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    if ($missing) {", ScRaw "        ($using:bad).Add(\"$base -- refused, but not with $missing (declared: $($codes -join ' '))\")", ScRaw "    } else {", ScRaw "        ($using:passed).Add($base)", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "}", ScBlank]

Section: S03

  s03 : List ShellCmd = [ScRaw "$sw.Stop()", ScRaw "$elapsed = [math]::Round($sw.Elapsed.TotalSeconds, 1)", ScBlank, ScRaw "if ($bad.Count -gt 0) {", ScRaw "    Write-Host ''", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"FAIL: $($bad.Count) of $($tests.Count) refusal test(s) did not refuse as declared:\"", ScRaw "    foreach ($b in ($bad | Sort-Object)) { Write-Host \"  $b\" }", ScRaw "    Write-Host ''", ScRaw "    Write-Host '  A test here asserts the compiler REFUSES a program, and what it refuses'", ScRaw "    Write-Host '  with is the assertion. A rejection that moved to a different code is a'", ScRaw "    Write-Host '  diagnostic regression; one that stopped happening is a soundness hole.'", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"  Per-test logs: $outRoot\\<name>\\<name>.log\"", ScRaw "    exit 1", ScRaw "}", ScBlank, ScRaw "$skipNote = if ($skipped.Count -gt 0) { \", $($skipped.Count) skipped\" } else { '' }", ScRaw "Write-Host \"  refusals ok ($($passed.Count) refused as declared$skipNote, ${elapsed}s)\"", ScRaw "foreach ($s in ($skipped | Sort-Object)) { Write-Host \"    skipped: $s\" }", ScRaw "exit 0"]

Section: Assembly

  ce-body : List ShellCmd = [ScSequence s01, ScSequence s02, ScSequence s03]

  ce-script : ShellScript = sh-script "check-errors" "every test under codex/test/errors must be REFUSED, with the codes it declares." ce-params ce-body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (emit-powershell ce-script)
  end

